# logs/paper/artifact_test_final.log
# Test of the final build of the supplementary archive (ttt6-artifact.tar.gz) after the second round of
# the internal refereeing.  The archive was unpacked into a fresh scratch directory, and the following was
# run there, in this order, with no other job on the machine:
#   sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256;  make bin/treecheck;  the certifying command of Section 8.3 of the paper;
#   python3 verify/spotcheck.py --selftest;  the exhaustive run of verify/spotcheck.py of Section 8.3
#   (--procs 4);  the verifier written from the paper alone (logs/paper/replication_from_paper/verify.cpp),
#   compiled and run on the certificate;  python3 logs/paper/referee/b_expand.py from the archive root;
#   logs/paper/lost_vectors/run.sh;  the three checks in logs/paper/round2_checks/;
#   logs/paper/check_refs.py;  scripts/check_7cube_midplanes.py;  a byte comparison of paper/paper.pdf in
#   the archive with paper/paper.pdf of the project;  a search of all text files of the archive and of
#   the text and the metadata of the two PDFs for names of products, companies or models of AI tools.
#
# Notes.
# (1) This log records the test of the build whose size and checksum are printed below.  The archive that
#     contains this log was built afterwards and differs from the tested build in exactly two files:
#     this log and MANIFEST.sha256.  The paper (sources and PDF), README.md, the programs, the
#     certificate and all other files are the same.
# (2) The reference running times of Section 8.3 and Appendix S6.2 of the paper and of README.md are taken
#     from the lines "real" and "user" below and from the logs of two earlier builds,
#     logs/paper/artifact_test.log and logs/paper/artifact_test_revision.log.  Running times vary by one
#     or two seconds from run to run.
# (3) The verifier written from the paper alone prints ACCEPT and reproduces all per-round counts, and
#     ends with exit code 1 ("1 mismatches"): besides verifying the certificate it compares its own
#     numbers of flows with two implementation statistics of the main verifier that were printed in the
#     first version of the paper (77,268 flows for pairs, 7,391 for triples); see Section 8.5 and
#     Appendix S4.1 of the paper.  Its full output is in logs/paper/replication_from_paper/run.log.
# (4) In the output file of the exhaustive run of verify/spotcheck.py the field "void_examples" (a list
#     of examples whose order depends on the scheduling of the processes) differs from
#     results/final/spotcheck_full.json, besides the fields that record the command line, the number of
#     processes and the times.  All counters agree.
# (5) logs/paper/referee/b_expand.py is run from the root of the unpacked archive; the archived copy
#     differs from the file in the project tree in the path of its output file, and b_sigma.py in the
#     path of the certificate (scripts/make_artifact.sh, "runnable copies").
#
